WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.580
In this video, you give a virtual machine a disk on NetApp ONTAP storage through the Trident CSI driver, then expand that disk while the virtual machine keeps running.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:20.630
Trident, the NetApp CSI driver, is installed on this cluster. Its storage class netapp-iscsi creates volumes on ONTAP over iSCSI.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:29.420
By default, SUSE Virtualization expands disks of running virtual machines only for Longhorn. The setting csi-online-expand-validation controls this.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.810
Open its action menu,

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.760
and select Edit Setting.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.100
Select Add.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:42.500
For the new provisioner, choose csi.trident.netapp.io,

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.520
and keep the value True.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.100
Select Save.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.660
Now create a virtual machine. On the Virtual Machines page, select Create.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.550
Choose the namespace demo,

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:57.930
and name it demo-netapp.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.920
Give it one CPU

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.260
and two gigabytes of memory.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.110
On the Volumes tab,

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:10.250
pick the openSUSE Leap image for the root disk. The root disk stays on Longhorn.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.570
Then select Add Volume for a data disk.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.510
Set its storage class to netapp-iscsi,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.820
and its size to one gigabyte.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:23.720
Select Create.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.710
Trident creates the volume on ONTAP, and the virtual machine is running.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:30.140
Open the virtual machine,

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.210
and its Volumes tab.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:39.970
The one gigabyte data disk comes from netapp-iscsi, a LUN on the NetApp storage system.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:45.960
Now grow the NetApp disk while the virtual machine runs. On the Volumes page, open its action menu,

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.590
and select Edit Config.

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:51.170
Change the size to two gigabytes.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:58.200
Select Save. Trident grows the LUN on ONTAP, and the virtual machine keeps running.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.970
The NetApp volume now shows two gigabytes.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:09.010
On the Virtual Machines page, demo-netapp is still running. The disk grew without a restart.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:16.749
The NetApp volume grew while the virtual machine kept running. Next, you fail over virtual machines to another cluster with harvey.
